WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:06.841
A settlement reader sends 200 postings to the ledger writer.

2
00:00:06.841 --> 00:00:09.647
A row lock holds the writer on posting 1.

3
00:00:09.647 --> 00:00:11.564
How far does the reader get?

4
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:14.688
With no buffer, emit calls the writer's code.

5
00:00:14.688 --> 00:00:18.168
The reader is stuck inside emit 1, so the count is 0.

6
00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:19.971
Add buffer(10).

7
00:00:19.971 --> 00:00:27.928
The reader moves to a second coroutine, in a room of its own, and its emits become sends onto a belt with 10 slots.

8
00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.855
The writer is still stuck.

9
00:00:29.855 --> 00:00:31.643
How many emits return now?

10
00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.128
Posting 1 rides the belt to the writer.

11
00:00:37.128 --> 00:00:39.476
Postings 2 to 11 fill the slots.

12
00:00:39.476 --> 00:00:43.145
Then the belt is full, and the next send suspends.

13
00:00:43.145 --> 00:00:43.659
Eleven.

14
00:00:43.933 --> 00:00:48.561
That's n plus 1: n on the belt, and one in the writer's hands.

15
00:00:48.561 --> 00:00:53.039
So buffer(0) gives 1, and buffer(), with 64 slots, gives 65.

16
00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:55.950
A full belt only makes the reader wait.

17
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.144
Nothing is lost.

18
00:00:58.733 --> 00:01:02.581
Now 200 FX ticks hit a repricer that is stuck on tick 1.

19
00:01:02.581 --> 00:01:06.498
conflate swaps the belt for a stand that holds one plate.

20
00:01:06.498 --> 00:01:08.353
What will the repricer see?

21
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.453
conflate never waits.

22
00:01:12.453 --> 00:01:17.782
Each new tick replaces the one on the stand, and the old one goes in the bin.

23
00:01:17.782 --> 00:01:20.065
The repricer sees only 1 and 200.

24
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:25.754
With collectLatest, a new tick cancels the repricing in progress.

25
00:01:25.754 --> 00:01:32.207
A tick every 100 milliseconds, 300 to reprice, and 50 to release a lock when cancelled.

26
00:01:32.207 --> 00:01:33.839
When does tick 3 come?

27
00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:39.779
At 200, tick 2 cancels repricing 1.

28
00:01:39.779 --> 00:01:45.362
Its cleanup runs until 250, and the feed waits inside emit.

29
00:01:45.362 --> 00:01:48.391
So tick 3 comes at 350, not 300.

30
00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:52.598
Picture a cashier who tears up a half-written receipt for each new order.

31
00:01:52.598 --> 00:01:57.443
She finishes shredding before she starts the next one, and the cook waits at the hatch.

32
00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.594
collectLatest cancels the old block, then joins it, inside the feed's emit.

33
00:02:03.594 --> 00:02:05.912
The run ends at 700, not 600.

34
00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.357
Each choice is one line.

35
00:02:08.357 --> 00:02:11.016
Reactor's closest twins are on the right.

36
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.357
So pick by what one lost value costs.

37
00:02:15.357 --> 00:02:17.154
FX repricing may conflate.

38
00:02:17.154 --> 00:02:21.439
Ledger postings must never drop: they get a buffer that waits.

39
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:22.418
Quick check.

40
00:02:22.418 --> 00:02:25.829
The writer is stuck on posting 1 behind buffer(1).

41
00:02:25.829 --> 00:02:27.807
How many emits have returned?
